  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 212 PM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nRidging over the Upper Midwest will continue to pull east\ntonight, with a shortwave lifting into the Northern Plains. That\nshortwave will head off into northern MN/Ontario tomorrow, with\nsouthwesterly flow aloft behind it into the upcoming weekend.\nAnother, stronger shortwave will come out into the region\nMonday, with the main upper trough axis arriving in the Rockies\nor western Plains by Tuesday. The second shortwave will help\npush an inverted surface trough and frontal boundary through the\nforecast area early next week. Near zonal to southwesterly flow\nsetting up for mid-week. After that the ensemble members are all\nover the place. The majority (37 percent) of the long range \nsolutions keep the Northern Plains in southwesterly flow aloft,\nbut there are a couple of other clusters with either broad\nridging or even northwesterly flow. With fairly high uncertainty\nwill keep the blended solution of low POPs and near average\ntemperatures. \n\n...Rain tonight/tomorrow and again Monday/Tuesday...\n\nShortwave will move in from the southwest tonight and provide\nsome lift for light rain to develop in warm air advection.\nHighest probability of rainfall amounts are around the tenth of\nan inch to perhaps a quarter of an inch range. However, with\nsome weak MU CAPE of up to 500 J/kg, can't completely rule out\nsome convective cells with heavier amounts. The decent pressure\ngradient will bring some fairly breezy winds and with showers\naiding mix down can't completely rule out some gusts up to 30\nmph or so at times. A bit of a break on Sunday, then the\nstronger system arrives early next week. Still some slight\nvariations in the exact track, but seem to be converging on a\nsolution with deformation band precipitation setting up over\nnortheastern ND and northwestern MN. Probabilities of amounts\nover 1 inch in this area are 60 to 70 percent, and there is even\nsome 20 to 30 percent probabilities of over 2 inches Monday into\nTuesday. A soaking rain seems likely, although could still be\nsome variations in exactly where the heaviest amounts set up\nbefore the period arrives.",
